WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.850
In 2023, Canada's wildfires released
almost 480 megatonnes of carbon.

2
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:13.010
Worldwide that year, wildfires
released an estimated 2,100 megatonnes.

3
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:18.990
Volcanoes add 130 to 380
million tonnes of CO₂ a year.

4
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.810
Over the ice ages of the
last million years or so,

5
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.590
CO₂ never rose above
300 parts per million.

6
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:31.010
By 2019, it was the highest
in at least 2 million years.

7
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:34.210
So what has changed the
carbon cycle so fast?

8
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.510
Bigger wildfires?

9
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.850
More eruptions?

10
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.250
In this mission, you'll weigh
natural and human changes,

11
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.610
from eruptions to farming
and deforestation.

12
00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:47.990
Then you'll balance the carbon
budget, and trace its impact on land,

13
00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.510
ocean and air.

14
00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:54.050
Your mission: explain what has
changed the carbon cycle so fast.
